Design recap (so the code below is self-consistent)
Job gets a new field panKeyLocation, generated once per job, in ChunkGeneratorController.postChunks — before dispatching any chunk.
That value is carried on every ChunkMessage via the existing encPanCsvPath field (no ChunkMessage schema change).
Stage 3 (SaveTriggeredConsumerDataImpl) and Stage 4 (FullfillerDefault) both read cm.getEncPanCsvPath() as the shared keyLocation and use the "always unknown, mint fresh index" substitution path.
Neither Stage 3 nor Stage 4 evicts PanSubstitutionService caches — they're shared across the whole job's lifetime.
Stage 5 (ShipfileBuilderImpl) reads job.getPanKeyLocation() directly (no more disk-scan-then-cache-lookup), builds the final ciphertext map, writes .out.EncPan.csv, and evicts caches for that keyLocation — this is the only place eviction happens.
